From 3719113013abaf5d212ae51024d8c90405a81efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:21:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2338/2409] drm/rockchip: vop2: Only vary the refresh rate with
 a VRR range

VRR_ENABLED is a property of every CRTC, so userspace can set it for any
output. The video port then stretches its frames to the vtotals of the
VRR state, which only the HDMI state helper fills in, and fails the
commit for a sink without VRR. An encoder that leaves the VRR state
empty (no VRR, or none for this mode) would get its frames set to a
vtotal of 0.

Treat a VRR state without a vtotal for the lowest refresh rate as a
fixed refresh rate, so that encoders can keep the refresh rate fixed for
modes or sinks without VRR by leaving the state cleared.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
index 67467184758e..aca0f01c051e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -3584,12 +3584,15 @@ static void vop2_crtc_atomic_flush(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 	spin_lock_irq(&crtc->dev->event_lock);
 
 	/*
-	 * VRR: the new frame is ready (the configuration is marked done
+	 * VRR, if the encoder set up a VRR range for the mode (it leaves the
+	 * VRR state cleared when the sink cannot vary the refresh rate of the
+	 * mode): the new frame is ready (the configuration is marked done
 	 * above), so end the stretched front porch of the current frame at the
 	 * earliest point (vop2_vp_end_vrr_frame()). The next
 	 * frame start stretches it again (vop2_vp_handle_vblank()).
 	 */
-	vp->vrr_active = vp->enabled && crtc_state->vrr_enabled;
+	vp->vrr_active = vp->enabled && crtc_state->vrr_enabled &&
+			 crtc_state->vrr_state.max_vtotal;
 	if (vp->vrr_active) {
 		vp->vrr_base_vtotal = crtc_state->vrr_state.base_vtotal;
 		vp->vrr_max_vtotal = crtc_state->vrr_state.max_vtotal;
-- 
